{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And you shall choose life.</b> The life of eternity." "<b>That you may live, you and your seed, loving HaShem your Elohim.</b> And I said that you should choose life — not as a hired servant working on condition to receive a reward. Rather, I said that you should choose what is truly life alone, so that you desire temporal life only for this end alone: that you love HaShem your Elohim, by recognizing His goodness together with the magnitude of His greatness."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:41.342174076Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}